e posts start coming in and  there's a post that says hey  we saw this guy at the intersection of  union street  and third avenue other twitter accounts  start to corroborate yeah  union street and third avenue and  minutes later  a facebook user whose real name is sean  patrick duff  shares this photo of what looks like the  exact same guy  lying unconscious on the ground with  other people looking on  there is video of the punch available  i'm not going to play it i don't think  it would add anything to the story  the man in the swastika armband can be  heard on the video  saying they deserve the welfare before  he's hit directly in the face by a guy  in a grey sweatshirt and subsequently  knocked unconscious  and immediately there's a whole bunch of  people who react to this  in the anti-fascist community  celebrating it absolutely loving it  the argument being made by people who  support the punching out of this guy  is listen he was harassing a black man  on the bus and this was merely a  response now  those against the punching out of this  guy say wait a second  we don't know if this guy was harassing  black people on the bus  the guy who did the punching certainly  wasn't one of the people on the bus who  could have witnessed that  and this is inappropriate violence now  of course this is against the law it's  not yet clear whether police are  involved in any way  i've been very clear about this issue i  do not believe it is okay  to punch nazis willy-nilly on a whim i'm  not saying this from some pie in the  sky the left should take the high road  type of position  i am saying i don't think it will  achieve anything  it might make neo-nazis scared to go out  in public wearing armbands  and that could maybe be seen as a  victory but from a pragmatic standpoint  it's not going to change the minds of  nazis to punch them in the face  if anything it's going to do the  opposite and it's going to be a feeding  frenzy for right-wing media for the  apologists to the so-called white  identity movement those who sympathize  with the ideology  we can have the moral debate and that  usually goes something like well  it's not okay to punch nazis because  they're not being physically violent and  then someone else says well  nazi ideology is violent so it's okay to  punch anyone who espouses it  the law happens not to agree with that  and the law is not always right  but i think the real problem here is the  pragmatic aspect of it this will not  achieve anything well i just think it's  completely counterproductive because you  take a guy like a neo-nazi  who obviously holds such deplorable  viewpoints and just about no one  sympathizing with him  and then you see him get punched out in  such a public way this video was put  online  and then just the national the natural  human emotion to respond to this is just  to express some sort of sympathy for him  we don't want him to be worthy of any of  our sympathy no let's not  make these individuals the victims and  from a practical perspective where do  you draw the line if nazi ideology is  violent enough for punching people in  the streets what about people who  advocate for the deportation of all  dreamers right kids who came to the u.s  underage and undocumented with their  parents that is major political violence  it is very violent  to send kids who came to the us through  no fault of their own back to a country  they may barely have a connection to  is it okay to punch people over that and  which people do we punch the politicians  who would vote in favor of that  or do we punch any random citizen who  supports the deportation of dreamers i  think it is very very problematic  and the bottom line is we don't aspire  to the same  values as nazis i don't anyway in  self-defense punch away  that has nothing to do with nazi views  anyone who's assaulting you  you are well within your rights to punch  away but  you have to take these arguments  sometimes to the extreme  to really understand why they don't make  sense and i actually read a comment  online saying hey  if no one punches nazis the holocaust  happens  that's a major slippery slope argument  right if i don't punch richard spencer  or this guy from seattle there's going  to be a holocaust we don't have to  resort to these tactics to achieve  social change period  and to be very clear i'm not in favor of  ignoring these people  you know that i've made it pretty clear  for a long time i don't subscribe to  that  but the movement to fight the resurgence  of neo-nazism or white supremacy  white separatism the white identity  movement call it what you want  it's not going to be toppled by  individuals who consider themselves  anti-fascist identifying an  armband-wearing dude  knocking him out and potentially getting  themselves arrested  it's just not going to be the right way  to approach this  the video you just watched was made  possible by support  from you please go to patreon.com  davidpakmanshow you can make a pledge of  as little as one dollar per month  and every dollar helps to support the  work that we're doing particularly in  light  of the youtube ad boycott which has been  really bad
 

